; The migration's two claims, re-asked as derivations (extension §2).
;
; Checked AGAINST migration.claims rather than replacing it: `pol check` answers
; `completes` and `no-dead-ends` with the checker's CTL reading, and
; modality-cross-check.sh re-asks the same two questions of the rules engine.
; Two implementations of one question; a disagreement is a bug in one of them.
;
; POLARITY — read this before "fixing" anything below.
;   `possible F` is encoded POSITIVELY: the relation holds the reachable
;   situations satisfying F, so NON-EMPTY means the property holds.
;   `live F` is AG EF F, which no stratified Datalog relation can say
;   positively, so it is encoded as its COUNTEREXAMPLE SET — the reachable
;   situations from which no F-situation is reachable. EMPTY means it holds.
;   Encoding `no-dead-ends` as "the situations that can still finish" would
;   read as the satisfying set and silently invert the oracle.
(load "ct.rules")

; The goal guard is written out longhand rather than reusing `contracted` from
; migration.lib.pol, and the reason is the file type: that library loads
; stdlib.pol, whose §3 and §7 SCHEMAS are declarations a rules file has no
; place for. river.rules writes its guard out for the same reason. The cost is
; one duplicated conjunction, and the cross-check is what keeps the copy
; honest — if this drifts from the claims file, the two engines disagree and
; the script goes red.
; `settled` is spelled with two LITERALS here — `(is prod.old r4)` rather than
; `(is prod.old prod.new)` — because a rules guard compares a chain against a
; literal, not against a second chain. It denotes the same set: the goal already
; pins `new` to r4, so "old equals new" and "old is r4" agree exactly here.
(satisfies completes
  (and (is name-col.state absent) (is prod.old r4) (is prod.new r4)))

; `live contracted`, as its complement: the situations from which the rename
; can no longer be finished. Empty ⟺ `holds no-dead-ends`.
(can-reach can-still-finish completes)
(trapped no-dead-ends can-still-finish)
